{
  "id": "same-word-added-twice",
  "title": "The same word is added on two devices offline",
  "covers": [
    "spec: Same word added twice offline - merged on the server by entry ID; cards and reviews combined",
    "ticket: same word added on two devices (merge)"
  ],
  "narrative": [
    "A has note W for 食べる with a meaning card and the mnemonic 'tabby eats' (T+10).",
    "B, offline, creates note L for the same entry at T+20 (sentence filled, meaning left empty), with a meaning and a reading card; tags it at T+30; suspends L's meaning card at T+31; reviews it at T+32.",
    "B pushes. note.created L collides with W: the server applies it, then emits note.merged L->W. Step 1 forwards fields.sentence@20; L's empty meaning has no clock and is not forwarded; W's mnemonic is kept.",
    "card.created (L, meaning) is applied to L, then merged into W's meaning card. card.created (L, reading): W has no reading card, so the server first creates one (ordinary card.created from the server device), then merges.",
    "B's later ops still address L and its cards. They are applied to the addressed row AND forwarded to the survivor: W gets the tags, W's meaning card is suspended.",
    "B's review keeps card_id = L's card; it is in the replay set of W's meaning card together with A's own review.",
    "B itself reaches the same state when it pulls the server-emitted ops: note.merged forwards L's clocked registers (sentence@20, tags@30), card.merged forwards suspended@31."
  ],
  "devices": {
